{"content_hash": "9b381940eee0ce5e", "version_id": 509, "article_id": 51, "level_code": "ja_n2", "lang": "ja", "level": 4, "level_label": "N2 中高級", "title": "ランセット委員会、AI悪用と核戦争が2100年までに人類滅亡の脅威と警告", "title_zh": "柳叶刀委员会警告：AI滥用与核战争或致人类在2100年前灭绝", "has_translation": true, "topic": "tech", "source": "guardian_tech", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2026/oct/11/nuclear-war-and-malicious-use-of-ai-threaten-end-of-humanity-by-2100-says-lancet-assessment", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1729284045177-7a40238e4cd0?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8NHx8bnVjbGVhciUyMHdhciUyMG1hbGljaW91c3xlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkxNjc3ODg3fDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Emanuel Kypreos on Unsplash", "author": "Emanuel Kypreos", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@mankip67?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-large-cloud-of-smoke-is-billowing-out-of-the-sky-XySaPZljJ54?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(260, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(298, 46%, 48%)", "label": "TECH", "seed": "6a7c012390e8"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-10", "word_count": 266, "reading_minutes": 0.9, "lead": "世界的な健康リスク評価により、AIの悪用や核戦争が今世紀末までに人類を絶滅させる可能性があることが示された。専門家らは17の脅威を特定し、対策の必要性を訴えている。", "lead_zh": "一项全球健康风险评估显示，AI滥用和核战争可能在本世纪末导致人类灭绝。专家们列出了17项威胁，并呼吁采取行动。", "preview": "ランセット委員会は、AIの悪用や核戦争が今後75年間で人類を絶滅させるリスクがあると報告した。核戦争による核の冬や、AIが作る生物兵器が大気を遮り飢饉を引き起こす可能性がある。ただし、その可能性は低いとしながらも、実現すれば人類に大災害をもたらすと警告している。", "preview_zh": "柳叶刀委员会报告称，AI滥用和核战争在未来75年内存在导致人类灭绝的风险。核战争可能引发核冬天，AI制造的生物武器可能遮蔽阳光并导致饥荒。尽管可能性较低，但一旦发生将给人类带来巨大灾难。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 497, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/51/ja_n2.mp3", "duration": 63.025, "size_bytes": 381888, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 176, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/509.json", "paragraphs": ["ランセット委員会は、AIの悪用や核戦争が今後75年間で人類を絶滅させるリスクがあると報告した。核戦争による核の冬や、AIが作る生物兵器が大気を遮り飢饉を引き起こす可能性がある。ただし、その可能性は低いとしながらも、実現すれば人類に大災害をもたらすと警告している。", "委員会は、健康被害を測る指標として障害調整生存年（DALY）を用い、17の主要な脅威を挙げた。大気汚染、薬剤耐性、子どもの栄養失調、気候変動、紛争、海外援助の削減、アルコール多飲、高血圧、所得格差、教育不足、自然発生のパンデミック、肥満、精神疾患、喫煙、不健康な加齢などが含まれる。", "これらの脅威は相互に関連しており、一緒に対処する必要がある。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["柳叶刀委员会报告称，AI滥用和核战争在未来75年内存在导致人类灭绝的风险。核战争可能引发核冬天，AI制造的生物武器可能遮蔽阳光并导致饥荒。尽管可能性较低，但一旦发生将给人类带来巨大灾难。", "委员会使用伤残调整生命年（DALY）衡量健康损失，列出了17项主要威胁，包括空气污染、抗微生物药物耐药性、儿童营养不良、气候变化、冲突、海外援助削减、酗酒、高血压、收入不平等、教育不足、自然大流行病、肥胖、精神疾病、吸烟和不健康老龄化。", "这些威胁相互关联，需要共同应对。委员会联合主席、华盛顿大学的克里斯托弗·默里教授表示：“今天领导人的决定将塑造下一代的健康与福祉。”他还强调，每项威胁都有“现实的行动路径”。"], "body": "ランセット委員会は、AIの悪用や核戦争が今後75年間で人類を絶滅させるリスクがあると報告した。核戦争による核の冬や、AIが作る生物兵器が大気を遮り飢饉を引き起こす可能性がある。ただし、その可能性は低いとしながらも、実現すれば人類に大災害をもたらすと警告している。\n\n委員会は、健康被害を測る指標として障害調整生存年（DALY）を用い、17の主要な脅威を挙げた。大気汚染、薬剤耐性、子どもの栄養失調、気候変動、紛争、海外援助の削減、アルコール多飲、高血圧、所得格差、教育不足、自然発生のパンデミック、肥満、精神疾患、喫煙、不健康な加齢などが含まれる。\n\nこれらの脅威は相互に関連しており、一緒に対処する必要がある。", "body_zh": "柳叶刀委员会报告称，AI滥用和核战争在未来75年内存在导致人类灭绝的风险。核战争可能引发核冬天，AI制造的生物武器可能遮蔽阳光并导致饥荒。尽管可能性较低，但一旦发生将给人类带来巨大灾难。\n\n委员会使用伤残调整生命年（DALY）衡量健康损失，列出了17项主要威胁，包括空气污染、抗微生物药物耐药性、儿童营养不良、气候变化、冲突、海外援助削减、酗酒、高血压、收入不平等、教育不足、自然大流行病、肥胖、精神疾病、吸烟和不健康老龄化。\n\n这些威胁相互关联，需要共同应对。委员会联合主席、华盛顿大学的克里斯托弗·默里教授表示：“今天领导人的决定将塑造下一代的健康与福祉。”他还强调，每项威胁都有“现实的行动路径”。", "text": "ランセット委員会は、AIの悪用や核戦争が今後75年間で人類を絶滅させるリスクがあると報告した。核戦争による核の冬や、AIが作る生物兵器が大気を遮り飢饉を引き起こす可能性がある。ただし、その可能性は低いとしながらも、実現すれば人類に大災害をもたらすと警告している。 委員会は、健康被害を測る指標として障害調整生存年（DALY）を用い、17の主要な脅威を挙げた。大気汚染、薬剤耐性、子どもの栄養失調、気候変動、紛争、海外援助の削減、アルコール多飲、高血圧、所得格差、教育不足、自然発生のパンデミック、肥満、精神疾患、喫煙、不健康な加齢などが含まれる。 これらの脅威は相互に関連しており、一緒に対処する必要がある。", "vocab": [{"word": "絶滅", "pos": "noun", "zh": "灭绝", "note": "指物种或人类的彻底消失", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "脅威", "pos": "noun", "zh": "威胁", "note": "常与「～となる」「～にさらされる」搭配", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "悪用", "pos": "noun", "zh": "滥用", "note": "如「AIの悪用」", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "核戦争", "pos": "noun", "zh": "核战争", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "飢饉", "pos": "noun", "zh": "饥荒", "note": "也写作「飢饉」", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "障害調整生存年", "pos": "noun", "zh": "伤残调整生命年", "note": "简称DALY，衡量健康寿命损失", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "大気汚染", "pos": "noun", "zh": "空气污染", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "薬剤耐性", "pos": "noun", "zh": "抗微生物药物耐药性", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "栄養失調", "pos": "noun", "zh": "营养不良", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "気候変動", "pos": "noun", "zh": "气候变化", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "所得格差", "pos": "noun", "zh": "收入不平等", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "パンデミック", "pos": "noun", "zh": "大流行病", "note": "外来语，指全球性传染病", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "精神疾患", "pos": "noun", "zh": "精神疾病", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "削減", "pos": "noun", "zh": "削减", "note": "如「援助の削減」", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Nuclear war and malicious use of AI threaten end of humanity by 2100, says Lancet assessment", "summary_original": "Newly established commission identifies 17 catastrophic threats to human health but says ‘realistic route to act’ on each exists\nHumans could become extinct by the year 2100 due to malicious use of AI or nuclear conflict, according to a new global risk assessment.\nThey top a list of 17 major threats to human health over the next 75 years, which also includes cuts to aid spending by wealthy countries, the climate crisis and childhood malnutrition.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "Nuclear war and malicious use of AI threaten end of humanity by 2100, says Lancet assessment\nNewly established commission identifies 17 catastrophic threats to human health but says ‘realistic route to act’ on each exists\nHumans could become extinct by the year 2100 due to malicious use of AI or nuclear conflict, according to a new global risk assessment.\nThey top a list of 17 major threats to human health over the next 75 years, which also includes cuts to aid spending by wealthy countries, the climate crisis and childhood malnutrition.\nThe experts behind\nThe Lancet Commission on 21st Century Global Threats to Health\nsaid all the threats interact, meaning they must be addressed together – but stressed that there was “a realistic route to act” on each.\n“Decisions made by leaders today will shape the health and wellbeing of the next generation,” said Prof Christopher Murray, commission co-chair and the director of the Institute for Health Metrics and Evaluation, University of Washington.\nTo create its list, the commission modelled how many years in good health might be lost due to sickness, disability or early deaths due to each threat, based on current trajectories – a measure known as disability-adjusted life years (Dalys).\n“Malicious use of AI, including bioweapons, and nuclear conflict with nuclear famine carry risks of extinction in the next 75 years,” the report said, adding that while their likelihood remained low, they had the potential to end humanity in the case of nuclear conflict by injecting enough particles into the upper atmosphere to block sunlight and cause famine, or via AI-created biological weapons. An accompanying Lancet editorial, published alongside the report, warned: “The scale of harm, should they be realised, would inflict an apocalypse on humanity.”\nOther risks that could cause more than 1bn cumulative Dalys, and therefore deemed “major catastrophic threats”, included\nair pollution\n,\nantimicrobial resistance\n,\nchildhood malnutrition\nand climate breakdown, as well as conventional conflict,\ndeclining overseas aid\n,\nhigh alcohol use\n, high blood pressure, income inequality, low educational attainment,\nnaturally occurring pandemics\n,\nobesity\n, poor\nmental health\n,\nsmoking\nand unhealthy\nageing\n.\nTo be included on the list, threats not only had to potentially cause a high number of lost healthy years, but also to have potential solutions.\nIbrahim Abubakar, commission member and professor of infectious disease epidemiology at UCL, said: “We are not starting from a point of view of ‘oh look, we want to scare you – we’ve got X many threats facing humanity’. We’re starting from the premise that if you are a policymaker today, whether at the global multilateral level or at the national level, these are the potential threats that you could face, and this is the magnitude by which, if you act, you can actually make a difference.”\nAction to limit\nglobal heating to about 1.8C (3.2F)\nrather than letting it reach 4.4C could prevent 1.89bn years of healthy life being lost, according to the report, which modelled best and worst case scenarios for each threat.\nIn higher income regions, non-communicable diseases such as obesity and poor mental health were the dominant threats, while in lower income regions health loss was driven by issues such as low educational attainment.\nMany major donor nations, including the US and UK, have announced\nlarge cuts to aid spending\nover the past year. The potential collapse of, or steep reduction in, international health aid could cause up to 1.5bn Dalys before 2100, the commission found, nearly 70% of which would be in sub-Saharan Africa. The region also bears the brunt of child malnutrition.\nThe commission was made up of 35 experts, and its findings will be shared on Sunday at the World Health Summit in Berlin, Germany. Their assessment will be updated annually to re-evaluate the 17 threats identified, incorporating new data and any emerging hazards.\nThe authors urged leaders to address the risks before they escalated into crises, including via investment in technological innovations and by strengthening health systems.\n“We started this process three years ago, thinking that there were three big threats: conflict, climate, and pandemics,” said Murray. “There’s a much larger number of threats that we need to worry about,